### Page content summary

| Section | Focus |
|--------|--------|
| **Purpose** | Catches perceived overload when `DET.CONTEXT.BURDEN` passes but the first viewport still feels noisy (PDCA framing) |
| **Passing signals** | One focal path (`product-landing-title` → `landing-hero-tagline` → CTAs); `landing-forge-visual` instead of hero-scale diagrams; outcome cards in the next `forge-section` |
| **Failing signals** | Stacked hero copy bands, dense `ks-diagram-tile` beside headline, three `forge-card` tiles competing in the same viewport |
| **Before example** | `landing_page` hero with all copy bands + architecture diagram + outcome cards in one viewport (≤ 3 buttons, still overwhelming) |
| **After example** | Staged hero with `landing-forge-visual`, outcome cards deferred, diagram in a labeled “How it works” section |
| **Evidence & remediation** | Screenshot capture steps + ordered remediation (collapse hero → defer diagram → section staging → ambient tuning → candidate `DET.*`) |

Uses real KS classes: `landing-hero-*`, `product-landing-title`, `forge-card`, `card-amber`, `forge-diagram`, `ks-diagram-tile`, `landing-forge-visual`, `forge-ambient--subtle`, hash attrs on sections.

